---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
import { FOUNDED, GEAR } from '../data/business';
---

<Page title="About" description="Meet Reliable Kev Media, a video production studio in North Jersey.">
  <h1>About Reliable Kev Media</h1>
  <figure class="pull">
    <img src="/images/vinny.jpg" alt="Vinny, owner of One Brick Media, at work in his shop" class="pull-photo" loading="lazy" />
    <div class="pull-text">
      <blockquote>Kev is at his best with just a camera and a chair.</blockquote>
      <figcaption>Vinny, owner of One Brick Media</figcaption>
    </div>
  </figure>
  <p>
    Reliable Kev Media is a video production studio filming across{' '}
    <a href="/where-i-work">{SITE.area}</a> since {FOUNDED}. We produce monthly content, podcasts and Q&As, events and brand films for
    towns, downtowns, local businesses and trade companies.
  </p>

  {/* Kev's own story (lightly cleaned up from his voice note). First person on purpose: this part is personal,
      unlike the rest of the site, which speaks as the studio ("we"). It used to be its own page (/meet-kev/,
      which now forwards here). */}
  <section id="meet-kev" class="meet-kev">
    <h2>Meet Kev</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      I have never been someone who's comfortable in front of the camera. Even recording myself, I've carried a sense
      of insecurity and self-doubt that I have always struggled with.
    </p>
    <figure class="single before">
      <img src="/images/kev-before-front.jpg" alt="Kev four years ago, flexing in his bedroom" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
    <p>
      Through my own effort, I've learned what it means to put yourself in a place where you have to trust yourself,
      and trust someone else to capture you.
    </p>
    <blockquote class="kev-pull">Trust yourself, and trust someone to capture you.</blockquote>
    <figure class="single">
      <img src="/images/kev-before-after.jpg" alt="Kev four years ago and today, side by side" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
    <p>
      That's where this is going, and it's why I tell other people's stories. I've never been someone who connects
      easily with groups. I connect with people one on one. That's why so much of my work is filming one-on-one with
      business owners, letting them tell their story.
    </p>
    <p>
      A lot of people just want help with their business. To me, that's not the right place to start. The approach I
      bring is the full context: how you started, and why you're doing this in the first place. Documentary style.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>The foundation</h2>
  <p>
    Reliable Kev Media did not come out of film school, an agency or a marketing firm. We do not sell ad campaigns
    or chase algorithms. What we bring is the ability to sit with someone, understand what matters to them and tell
    that story clearly.
  </p>
  <p>
    That is the foundation of Reliable Kev Media. Every project begins with listening. The direction, the shots and
    the edit all follow from your story, not from a template.
  </p>
  <p>
    In every business we film, we look for the whole arc: where you started, the work it took and where you are going.
  </p>

  <h2>Behind the camera</h2>
  <div class="bts">
    <figure class="bts-wide"><img src="/images/kev-filming-kneeling.jpg" alt="Kev kneeling to frame a shot at an outdoor event" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    <figure><img src="/images/kev-filming-event.jpg" alt="Kev filming dogs and their owners at an outdoor event" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    <figure><img src="/images/kev-fitness-shoot.jpg" alt="Kev with a client on set at a fitness shoot" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    <figure><img src="/images/kev-camera-screen.jpg" alt="A camera screen mid-recording, framing a detail shot" loading="lazy" /></figure>
  </div>

  <h2>Full context storytelling</h2>
  <p>
    We invest the time, care and thought to understand your story, then direct and shape it on camera. Trust is the
    most valuable thing a business has, and people want to see who they are hiring before they call. That is why we
    never film just the product. Every project tells three stories:
  </p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>The business.</strong> What you make, how you work, and why customers keep coming back.</li>
    <li><strong>The owner.</strong> Your story, in your words, so people know who they are buying from.</li>
    <li><strong>The town.</strong> The street, the neighbors, the community you are part of.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we work with</h2>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>Towns and municipalities showing residents what is being built, fixed and planned</li>
    <li>Downtowns and chambers of commerce that want people walking their streets</li>
    <li>Local shops, restaurants and services</li>
    <li>Trades and contractors: concrete, construction, landscaping and more</li>
  </ul>

  {/* Community section returns once Kev shares the local work he does. */}

  <h2>The gear</h2>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>{GEAR.cameras}, so interviews and podcasts are covered from two angles</li>
    <li>{GEAR.support}</li>
    <li>{GEAR.drone} for aerial footage</li>
  </ul>
  <figure class="clip">
    <video src="/videos/about-flying.mp4" poster="/videos/about-flying.jpg" muted loop playsinline autoplay preload="metadata" data-autoplay aria-label="Flying the drone at an event in Park Ridge"></video>
  </figure>

  <h2>Our standards for quality</h2>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>A plan before every shoot, so nothing is wasted</li>
    <li>Respect for your time, your crew and your customers on shoot day</li>
    <li>Clean edits delivered on schedule, ready to post</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/start">Book a free call</a> and let's talk about your story.</p>
</Page>

<style>
  /* Meet Kev: Kev's story, told in the first person. */
  .meet-kev { max-width: 680px; scroll-margin-top: 110px; }
  .meet-kev p { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .meet-kev .lead { font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.4vw, 1.4rem); color: var(--text) !important; }
  .single { margin: 32px 0; }
  .single img { width: 100%; display: block; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .before { max-width: 340px; }
  .kev-pull {
    margin: 32px 0; padding: 4px 0 4px 22px; border-left: 3px solid var(--red);
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.9rem); line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .clip { margin: 20px 0 0; max-width: 640px; }
  .clip video { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; display: block; background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  /* Vinny's quote over his photo: full width, darkened toward the left so the words read. */
  .pull { position: relative; margin: 0 0 40px; min-height: clamp(340px, 46vw, 500px); display: flex; align-items: flex-end; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--glass-line); border-radius: var(--media-radius); }
  .pull-photo { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 60% 6%; }
  .pull::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1; background: linear-gradient(to right, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.85), rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55) 50%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1)), linear-gradient(to top, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6), transparent 60%); }
  .pull-text { position: relative; z-index: 2; padding: clamp(22px, 4vw, 40px); max-width: 36ch; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .pull::before { background: linear-gradient(to top, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9), rgb(0 0 0 / 0.35) 75%); } .pull-text { max-width: none; } }
  .pull blockquote { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2vw, 2.2rem); text-shadow: 0 2px 14px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5); line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
  .pull blockquote::before { content: '\201C'; }
  .pull blockquote::after { content: '\201D'; }
  .pull figcaption { margin-top: 12px; font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text); opacity: 0.85; }
  .photo { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--glass-line); border-radius: var(--media-radius); display: grid; place-items: center; margin: 28px 0; }
  /* Behind-the-scenes photos: one wide shot, then three tall ones in a row. */
  .bts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .bts figure { margin: 0; }
  .bts img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; object-fit: cover; display: block; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .bts .bts-wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .bts .bts-wide img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-position: 50% 60%; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .bts { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .bts figure:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .bts figure:last-child img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; }
  }
</style>
